  <section id="target-market" class="home-focus-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-label">Ideal customer profile and target market</div>
      <h2>Before the calling starts, we get clear on who is worth calling.</h2>
      <p>A larger list is not automatically a better list. We first clarify the type of company that can realistically buy the offer and the people most likely to understand the problem. That may include industry, location, company size, business model, technology, operating condition, role, seniority, and obvious reasons the account may or may not fit.</p>
      <p>We also agree on exclusions. A campaign should not waste time calling companies that are too small, too large, in the wrong region, outside the required industry, already active customers, direct competitors, students, vendors, or roles that cannot move the conversation forward.</p>
      <div class="home-inline-checks"><span>Best-fit companies</span><span>Right decision-makers</span><span>Clear exclusions</span><span>Useful call reason</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

