      <h2>See the work, the outcomes, and what the market is teaching us.</h2>
      <p>Activity matters, but activity alone does not explain performance. Reporting can include calls, connection outcomes, call dispositions, wrong-person results, referrals, objections, qualification notes, follow-up status, meetings booked, and other agreed campaign measures.</p>
      <p>The more valuable layer is the market response. Are the right people answering? Do they understand the problem? Is the role wrong? Does one industry respond better? Is the offer arriving too early, too late, or with weak language? Are meetings being lost because of targeting, data, message, timing, or qualification?</p>
