  <section id="faq" class="home-faq-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">Frequently asked questions</div>
      <h2>Questions about outbound calling and appointment setting.</h2>
      <div class="home-faq-list">
        <details><summary>Can CallTeam build the prospect list?</summary><p>Yes. CallTeam can build a targeted B2B prospect list around the companies, industries, locations, company sizes, and decision-maker roles that fit your offer. We can also verify and refine a list you already have.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can CallTeam call a list we already have?</summary><p>Yes. If you already have a prospect list, CRM contacts, target accounts, or leads from another source, CallTeam can organize the calling plan, make the calls, follow up, qualify responses, and book appropriate conversations.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can you call old CRM leads?</summary><p>Yes. CallTeam can work through old CRM leads, dormant opportunities, previous inquiries, no-decisions, and contacts that stopped responding. We agree on the priority, message, status rules, and handoff before outreach starts.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can you follow up with inbound, event, or webinar leads?</summary><p>Yes. CallTeam can follow up with inbound form leads, demo requests, event lists, trade-show contacts, webinar attendees, referrals, and other warm or time-sensitive leads. The campaign is built around the source and the reason the person entered the list.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is outbound calling the same as cold calling?</summary><p>Cold calling is one type of outbound calling. Outbound calling can also include old-lead reactivation, inbound lead follow-up, event follow-up, target-account outreach, referral follow-up, and calls to prospects who have already shown some interest.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How do callers represent our company, and who approves the talk track?</summary><p>Callers work from an agreed campaign brief and represent the client in the way approved before launch. The client reviews the core talk track, positioning, qualification questions, meeting standard, and important boundaries. Real conversations then help refine the language.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How does CallTeam research prospects?</summary><p>Research depends on the campaign. It can include company fit, industry, size, location, decision-maker role, available contact data, account changes, relevant business signals, CRM history, and public context that helps the caller understand why the account may be worth contacting.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How does CallTeam qualify a meeting?</summary><p>Qualification criteria are agreed before launch. They can include company fit, role relevance, need, interest, timing, current approach, decision path, and a clear reason for a next conversation. The exact standard should match the offer and sales process.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What information comes with a booked meeting?</summary><p>The handoff can include the contact and company, why the conversation was booked, useful call notes, relevant needs or objections, timing, people involved, and the agreed next step. The exact fields are set during campaign setup.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can CallTeam work inside our CRM?</summary><p>CallTeam can work with an agreed CRM or campaign workflow when access, permissions, fields, and operating rules are clear. If direct CRM work is not appropriate, we can agree on another clean reporting and handoff process.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What reporting do we receive?</summary><p>Reporting is matched to the engagement and can include activity, connection outcomes, call dispositions, objections, referrals, qualification notes, follow-up status, meetings booked, and market feedback. The goal is to show what happened and what the campaign is learning.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How much calling volume is included?</summary><p>Calling volume depends on list size, research needs, contact quality, follow-up depth, market, talk-track complexity, and campaign goals. CallTeam scopes the right operating level after reviewing the work instead of forcing every client into one activity package.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How long does campaign setup take?</summary><p>Setup time depends on how clear the offer, target market, list, data, talk track, CRM process, and qualification rules already are. A focused campaign with approved inputs can move faster than a campaign that needs targeting and list building from the ground up.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How is CallTeam pricing determined?</summary><p>Pricing depends on the campaign scope, list and research work, calling and follow-up needs, reporting, systems, market complexity, and level of management required. A strategy call is used to understand the work before a recommendation is made.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is CallTeam an outsourced SDR service or a call centre?</summary><p>CallTeam can provide the front-end work many companies expect from an outsourced SDR service, including prospecting, calling, follow-up, qualification, and appointment setting. It is not positioned as a generic high-volume call centre. The work is built around the client's offer, market, qualification standard, and sales handoff.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How does AI support the outbound calling process?</summary><p>AI can support account research, list enrichment, lead prioritization, call preparation, message comparison, note organization, and campaign learning. Experienced people make the calls, listen, respond, qualify, and use judgment in the live conversation.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does CallTeam guarantee appointments?</summary><p>No honest provider can control every buyer, list, market, offer, timing issue, or competitive condition. CallTeam builds and runs the agreed process, measures the work, shares what the market is saying, and improves the campaign using real evidence. Specific commercial commitments belong in the engagement agreement.</p></details>
        <details><summary>When is CallTeam not the right fit, and which offer should we choose?</summary><p>Done-for-you outbound calling fits when you need leads sourced or a list called, followed up, qualified, and booked. Sales Execution Lab fits when your own people need better sales behavior. The 90-Day Revenue Engine fits when the whole pipeline system needs structure. CallTeam may not be the right fit when the offer is still unproven, the target market cannot be defined, or the goal is only the cheapest possible call volume.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

